{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-08-Jan-2026-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The age of T is 20 years more than the age of R. S's age is 10 years less than the age of P. P's age is half the age of R. The sum of ages of all is 130 years. What is the age of R in years?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "direct-inverse-variation", "key_answer": "18"}, {"n": 3, "text": "3206", "options": [{"text": "19 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "26 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "29 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "34 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "19"}, {"n": 4, "text": "What is the mode of the following data? 47, 51, 51, 48, 53, 54, 47, 52, 51, 46, 43, 47, 52, 40, 47, 41, 43, 43, 46, 474284", "options": [{"text": "43", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "47"}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "9"}, {"n": 6, "text": "The amount on a sum of ₹1,200 at 15% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, in 2 years will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹1,846", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,725", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,646", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,587", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹1,587"}, {"n": 7, "text": "Ravi buys a shirt with a marked price of ₹1,620. He receives two successive discounts of 20% and 10%. Calculate the price Ravi paid for the shirt.4360", "options": [{"text": "₹1,260.45", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,166.40", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,288.25", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,330.50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹1,166.40"}, {"n": 8, "text": "3206", "options": [{"text": "19 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "26 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "29 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "34 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "26 km/hr"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The sum of two numbers is 45. One number is 5 more than the other. Find the larger number.", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": "25"}, {"n": 10, "text": "₹1,411 is divided among Pooja, Harsh and Madhur in such a way that if ₹12, ₹23 and ₹43 are deducted from their respective shares, they have money in the ratio 21:16:6. Find the actual share of Harsh.", "options": [{"text": "₹596", "added": false}, {"text": "₹519", "added": false}, {"text": "₹646", "added": false}, {"text": "₹546", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "₹519"}, {"n": 11, "text": "In quadrilateral PQRS, the bisectors of ∠ R and ∠ S meet at the point T (inside the quadrilateral) and ∠ STR = 44°. If the ratio of ∠ P to ∠ Q is 5 : 6, then what is the difference between the measures of ∠ Q and ∠ P?", "options": [{"text": "5°", "added": false}, {"text": "7°", "added": false}, {"text": "8°", "added": false}, {"text": "13°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "8°"}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "16"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The marked price of a washing machine is ₹62,000. A shopkeeper allows a discount of 73% and gets a profit of 20%. What is the cost price of the washing machine?", "options": [{"text": "₹13,966", "added": false}, {"text": "₹13,950", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,058", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,038", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹13,950"}, {"n": 14, "text": "The curved surface area and the height of a right circular cylinder are 924 cm2and 14 cm, respectively. Find its diameter (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": "21"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The monthly incomes of two friends David and Ashish, are in the ratio 5 : 9, respectively, and each of them saves ₹39,000 every month. If the ratio of their monthly expenditure is 2 : 4, find the monthly income of David (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "1,94,000", "added": false}, {"text": "2,73,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,96,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,95,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "1,95,000"}, {"n": 16, "text": "A ladder 10 metres long leans against a wall making an angle of 60° with the ground. Find the height (in metres) of the wall the ladder reaches. Ans A. B. C. D.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "heights-and-distances", "key_answer": "D"}, {"n": 17, "text": "P and Q together can fill a cistern with water in 9 hours. If P alone can fill the cistern with water in 36 hours, then in how many hours will Q alone fill one-fourth of the same cistern with water?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "fill-empty", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Due to water crisis, 40% of the initial population left the village, and 10% of the remaining left the town for pursuing jobs. If presently, 1080 people inhabit the village, what is the ratio of the initial population to the present population?", "options": [{"text": "57:32", "added": false}, {"text": "50:27", "added": false}, {"text": "52:32", "added": false}, {"text": "50:23", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": "50:27"}, {"n": 19, "text": "A cistern has a hole at the bottom through which water leaks. A tap can fill the cistern in 9 hours and the hole at the bottom can empty the fully filled cistern in 12 hours. If both the tap and the hole are open, then what will be the time taken to completely fill the empty cistern?", "options": [{"text": "33.3 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "27 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "36 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "29.9 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "leak", "key_answer": "36 hours"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Find a single discount (approximately) equal to three consecutive discounts of 22%, 8% and 17%.", "options": [{"text": "42.91%", "added": false}, {"text": "43.38%", "added": false}, {"text": "43.24%", "added": false}, {"text": "40.44%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": "40.44%"}, {"n": 21, "text": "The fourth proportional to 20, 15 and 8 is the same as the third proportional to A and 30. What is the value of A?", "options": [{"text": "147", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "148", "added": false}, {"text": "153", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "150"}, {"n": 22, "text": "What is the greatest volume container (in litres) that can measure 300 litres, 280 litres and 180 litres.", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "20"}, {"n": 23, "text": "Find the number of bricks required to build a wall 20 m long, 9.9 m high and 30 cm thick, using bricks of size 25 cm × 11 cm × 8 cm, if 10% of the wall volume is filled with cement.", "options": [{"text": "26,500", "added": false}, {"text": "25,800", "added": false}, {"text": "30,200", "added": false}, {"text": "24,300", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "24,300"}, {"n": 24, "text": "A shopkeeper marks his goods at 40% above the cost price. He then offers a discount of 20% on the marked price. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "12%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "12%"}, {"n": 25, "text": "A car travels 187 km in the first hour and 273 km in the second hour. What is the average speed (in km/hr) of the car for the whole journey?", "options": [{"text": "223", "added": false}, {"text": "231", "added": false}, {"text": "222", "added": false}, {"text": "230", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "230"}]}